.Sh NAME
.Nm bge
.Nd "Encrypt files and folders with someone's key or a password. An open .bge format, secured with RSA-4096 + AES-256-GCM."
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar subcommand
.Op Fl -version
.Op Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Get started:
  bge keygen -o alice                       create alice.pem + alice.pub.pem
  bge encrypt report.pdf -r alice.pub.pem   encrypt for alice  report.pdf.bge
  bge decrypt report.pdf.bge -k alice.pem   decrypt back to report.pdf
  bge encrypt report.pdf -p                 use a password instead of a key
  bge encrypt myfolder -a -r alice.pub.pem  zip+encrypt  myfolder.zip.bge
  bge inspect report.pdf.bge                show its mode/size (no key needed)

Encrypt by name (saved keys live in ~/.bge):
  bge contact add alice.pub.pem -n Alice    save a friend's public key
  bge identity add me.pub.pem -n Me         register your own identity
  bge encrypt report.pdf -r Alice           encrypt to a saved contact
  bge encrypt report.pdf                    no -r  your active identity

Run 'bge <command> -h' for the examples and every option of each command.
